cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: "Products of exact prime-race crossing heights"
abstract: "At the exact amplitude 1.9735, the 62 crossing heights through one million and the eleven primes through 31 have no nontrivial product relation with exponents bounded by 90,000. Two opposite-sign crossing pairs have transcendental geometric midpoints. The proof determines the generic multiplicative rank and gives an arithmetic alternative for every fixed positive magnitude through 5.85."
